      "text": "(\n    <div style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--color-background)', boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', fontSize: '12px', fontSynthesis: 'none', gap: '40px', height: 'fit-content', lineHeight: '16px', MozOsxFontSmoothing: 'grayscale', overflow: 'clip', overflowWrap: 'anywhere', padding: '48px', WebkitFontSmoothing: 'antialiased', width: '1280px' }}>\n      <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '8px' }}>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-foreground)', display: 'inline-block', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '30px', fontWeight: 600, letterSpacing: '-0.025em', lineHeight: '36px' }}>\n          AppSidebar\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-muted-foreground)', display: 'inline-block', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '16px', lineHeight: '24px', width: '820px' }}>\n          The desktop sidebar: 248px wide, 16px padding, a soft right border and no brand block. Five links (For You, Your Songs, Wallet, Notifications, Profile), a Communities section, a Moderator section when the viewer moderates something, and the account row pinned to the bottom behind a divider. The account row shows the profile in use and opens the account menu (Parts/Shell/AppShellChrome), per the workspace_owner on 2026-10-12; its second line, the profile's community, is the design agent's choice. Notifications carries a dot when something is unread, and never when signed out. The create-community plus belongs to the Communities header row, right-aligned and centred on the label; it is never a standalone button. Links are 40px rows with 12px radius; community rows are 44px with a 24px coloured avatar. There is no Post here: a post belongs to a community, so Post lives on the community page.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div style={{ alignItems: 'start', boxSizing: 'border-bo